  "decision": "Keep FFTE default; optional rvv10_fft=fftw. Current FFTW packing dominates the larger-grid transform and provides no consistent whole-functional speedup.",
  "limitations": [
    "Single local machine, 2/4 ranks; no production water or multinode scaling measurement.",
    "FFTE includes per-transform private-table initialization; this is an implemented-path comparison, not an intrinsic FFT library comparison.",
    "Backend order is fixed in each timing trial; timing variation can affect whole-functional comparisons.",
    "FFTW cache calls are nonreentrant and require consistent collective arguments and coordinate-ordered communicators.",
    "Fortran allocations do not recover collectively from allocation failure. Existing distributed allocations precede the new transform size guard; there is no end-to-end huge-grid overflow guarantee.",
    "Direct potential assembly uses periodic shifts; native halo derivatives are covered by the LCFO fixtures.",
    "DC-MD remains unsupported."
  ],
